{"name":"Floral Arrangement","hex":"#c6ac9f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"floral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, or connected with flowers.","Portraying flowers, especially in a stylized way."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A design involving flowers","A perfume redolent of flowers"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floral"},{"term":"arrangement","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of arranging.","The manner of being arranged."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrangement"}],"entries":[{"title":"Floral design","blocks":[{"text":"Floral design or flower arrangement is the art of using plant material and flowers to create an eye-catching and balanced composition or display. Evidence of refined floral design is found as far back as the culture of ancient Egypt. Floral designs, called arrangements, incorporate the five elements and seven principles of floral design."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Lady_arranging_flower_bouquet_Tokyo_1930s.jpg/330px-Lady_arranging_flower_bouquet_Tokyo_1930s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floral_design"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"},{"title":"Arrangement","blocks":[{"text":"In music, an arrangement is a musical adaptation of an existing composition. Differences from the original composition may include reharmonization, melodic paraphrasing, orchestration, or formal development. Arranging differs from orchestration in that the latter process is limited to the assignment of notes to instruments for performance by an orchestra, concert band, or other musical ensemble. Arranging \"involves adding compositional techniques, such as new thematic material for introductions, transitions, or modulations, and endings. Arranging is the art of giving an existing melody musical variety\". In jazz, a memorized (unwritten) arrangement of a new or pre-existing composition is known as a head arrangement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Fliegende_Hollander_Wagner_Sousa_25.jpg/330px-Fliegende_Hollander_Wagner_Sousa_25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrangement"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Floral_Display_Congregational_Chapel%2C_Fore_Street%2C_Beer%2C_Devon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4180232.jpg/500px-Floral_Display_Congregational_Chapel%2C_Fore_Street%2C_Beer%2C_Devon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4180232.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Floral_Display_Congregational_Chapel%2C_Fore_Street%2C_Beer%2C_Devon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4180232.jpg/500px-Floral_Display_Congregational_Chapel%2C_Fore_Street%2C_Beer%2C_Devon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4180232.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An arrangement displayed at a church in Beer, United Kingdom","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFloral_Display_Congregational_Chapel%